            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "The path gets lost because LSP completion rebuilds the whole list. It gets the current items via complete_info(), merges in the LSP matches, and calls complete() again. But complete_info() only exports the menu text (cp_text[CPT_MENU]), not cp_fname, where buffer paths are stored. So buffer items lose their path when complete() rebuilds the list.\n\nhttps://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/2accbdfd42447c691f685d20b719eec350a875f3/runtime/lua/vim/lsp/completion.lua#L1169-L1180\n\n\nBut the test seems a bit off from what the issue describes... \n\n```diff\ndiff --git a/test/functional/editor/completion_spec.lua b/test/functional/editor/completion_spec.lua\nindex 04b284c06b..519399cfb3 100644\n--- a/test/functional/editor/completion_spec.lua\n+++ b/test/functional/editor/completion_spec.lua\n@@ -1972,4 +1972,13 @@ describe('completion', function()\n     eq('(', items[3].commit_chars)\n     eq({ nil, nil, nil }, { items[4].equal, items[4].preselect, items[4].commit_chars })\n   end)\n+\n+  it('complete_info() reports the source file name of item', function()\n+    command('set hidden complete=b completeopt=menuone,noselect')\n+    command('file Xcompletion-source')\n+    api.nvim_buf_set_lines(0, 0, -1, false, { 'foobar' })\n+    command('enew')\n+    feed('ifoo<C-n>')\n+    eq('Xcompletion-source', fn.complete_info({ 'items' }).items[1].menu)\n+  end)\n end)\ndiff --git a/test/functional/plugin/lsp/completion_spec.lua b/test/functional/plugin/lsp/completion_spec.lua\nindex 113f779538..f3666a53f3 100644\n--- a/test/functional/plugin/lsp/completion_spec.lua\n+++ b/test/functional/plugin/lsp/completion_spec.lua\n@@ -1997,8 +1997,16 @@ describe(\"vim.lsp.completion: omnifunc + 'autocomplete'\", function()\n   end\n\n   it('merges with other completions', function()\n-    feed('ihillo<cr><esc>ih')\n+    local bufname = exec_lua(function()\n+      vim.o.complete = 'o,b'\n+      local buf = vim.api.nvim_create_buf(true, false)\n+      vim.api.nvim_buf_set_name(buf, 'Xcompletion-source')\n+      vim.api.nvim_buf_set_lines(buf, 0, -1, false, { 'hillo' })\n+      return vim.fn.bufname(buf)\n+    end)\n+    feed('ih')\n     assert_matches({ 'hillo', 'hallo', 'hello' })\n+    eq(bufname, exec_lua('return vim.fn.complete_info({ \"items\" })').items[1].menu)\n   end)\n\n   it('fuzzy matches without duplication', function()\n```\n\n",
            "commit_id": "fcc855e6c10b26c1668226bfb8e993ed7a960f28",
            "created_at": "2026-10-15T15:18:51Z",
            "diff_hunk": "@@ -3691,7 +3691,9 @@ static void fill_complete_info_dict(dict_T *di, compl_T *match, bool add_match)\n {\n   tv_dict_add_str_len(di, S_LEN(\"word\"), match->cp_str.data, (int)match->cp_str.size);\n   tv_dict_add_str(di, S_LEN(\"abbr\"), match->cp_text[CPT_ABBR]);\n-  tv_dict_add_str(di, S_LEN(\"menu\"), match->cp_text[CPT_MENU]);\n+  // Preserve the filename fallback displayed in the popup menu when items are reused.\n+  tv_dict_add_str(di, S_LEN(\"menu\"), match->cp_text[CPT_MENU] != NULL\n+                  ? match->cp_text[CPT_MENU] : match->cp_fname);",
